# test-guest.env — the single source of truth for every pinned value the
# local test-guest rig depends on. build-test-guest.sh, boot-test-guest.sh, and
# verify-test-guest.sh all read THIS file; IMAGE-IDENTITY.md quotes the same
# values in prose and verify-test-guest.sh enforces that the doc and this file
# agree (token-for-token), so a pin bump is one reviewed diff that cannot drift
# the doc out from under it.
#
# This file is POSIX-sourced (KEY=value, no spaces around `=`) and also grepped
# by verify-test-guest.sh, so keep one pin per line with the exact
# `TG_<NAME>=<value>` shape.
#
# WHAT THIS IMAGE IS (and is NOT). This is a LIGHTWEIGHT TEST FIXTURE for the
# sudo-free qemu rig — a small, pinned, sha256-verified bootable guest used to
# exercise the boot/network path locally. It is explicitly NOT the heavyweight
# images/golden/ M0 session image (glibc/Debian + pinned Claude Code, D49) that
# vm/m0-image/ hand-builds; that image stands on its own. A musl/Alpine fixture
# is fine here precisely because nothing in this tree resolves through
# ds-dnsgate's ask path (the doc 11 §8.6 musl-REFUSED adjudication is about the
# PRODUCTION guest userland, not a local boot fixture).
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

# --- Base image: pinned Alpine "nocloud" cloud qcow2 (version + sha256) ---
# Alpine nocloud cloud image: a complete, small bootable userland that auto-
# consumes a NoCloud cloud-init seed (DataSourceNoCloud). The base image does
# NOT preinstall curl, so the generated seed's runcmd `apk add --no-cache curl`
# ensures it at first boot (the recorded boot-smoke; see BUILD-NOTES.md). The
# `bios-cloudinit` flavor (SeaBIOS boot, cloud-init present) is what the rig
# needs: SeaBIOS is bundled with the sudo-free qemu, and cloud-init lets the
# generated seed set the static 10.77.0.x address + hostname + autologin.
TG_ALPINE_VERSION=3.21.7
TG_ALPINE_ARCH=x86_64
TG_ALPINE_FLAVOR=bios-cloudinit-r0
TG_IMAGE_NAME=nocloud_alpine-3.21.7-x86_64-bios-cloudinit-r0.qcow2
# CDN base. Fetch with `curl --noproxy '*'` — a global HTTPS_PROXY=:18080 breaks
# non-API egress, so the builder always passes --noproxy for the image fetch.
TG_IMAGE_BASE_URL=https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/v3.21/releases/cloud

# --- Integrity pins (verified after download, build fails closed on mismatch) ---
# sha256 is THE pin this builder enforces (the task's "sha256-verified"
# contract). It was computed from the authentic image whose sha512 matched
# Alpine's own published `<image>.sha512` sidecar (recorded in BUILD-NOTES.md),
# so the sha256 pin chains to Alpine's signed-release integrity statement.
TG_IMAGE_SHA256=17bdcba6c3cf1694d3d6f841acc0ec87dc201aef3dca2673f2f948b401c1e516
# Alpine publishes a `<image>.sha512` sidecar (no `.sha256`); the builder ALSO
# verifies against this when reachable as a second, vendor-published check.
TG_IMAGE_SHA512=5b22a46e9aa6bbacf585c055e87362c8be1993e53c121bdaf74203ac3490c70bdbbf714df4276eef36184ea8c11fd7cd3b28c9ccc74f6a9a82c430d441fa2f95

# --- Static network config (doc 13 §3 / §4 per-session-tap addressing) ---
# The TAP-mode addressing the generated NoCloud network-config applies inside
# the guest. The dstap-0 attach is the SEPARATE §E2 task (needs sudo to create
# the tap on the host); this rig only bakes the guest-side static config and
# supports BOTH a user-net smoke and a tap mode at boot. The gateway/DNS is the
# boundary host's per-session-tap address (the in-guest belt to ds-dnsgate).
TG_GUEST_IP=10.77.0.2
TG_GUEST_CIDR=24
TG_GUEST_GATEWAY=10.77.0.1
TG_GUEST_DNS=10.77.0.1
# The host-side tap the tap-mode boot attaches to (created by the §E2 task).
TG_TAP_IFNAME=dstap-0
# The smoke target the in-guest self-assert curls (an upstream the user-net
# slirp gateway can always reach; a plain-text small object over TLS).
TG_SMOKE_URL=https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/MIRRORS.txt

# --- qemu rig (sudo-free user qemu) ---
# The sole sanctioned local runtime for this unit: the sudo-free qemu under
# ~/.local/opt/qemu (qemu 11), KVM via the 0666 /dev/kvm (TCG fallback). The
# boot wrapper exports LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$TG_QEMU_LIB and runs $TG_QEMU_BIN.
TG_QEMU_PREFIX=${HOME}/.local/opt/qemu
TG_QEMU_LIB=${HOME}/.local/opt/qemu/usr/lib
TG_QEMU_BIN=${HOME}/.local/opt/qemu/usr/bin/qemu-system-x86_64
TG_QEMU_SHARE=${HOME}/.local/opt/qemu/usr/share/qemu
# Guest resources for the boot smoke (small — this is a fixture).
TG_GUEST_MEM_MB=768
TG_GUEST_SMP=2

# --- Scratch/output layout (btrfs CoW under ~/tmp, NEVER /tmp, NEVER the repo) ---
# All blobs (qcow2, seed ISO) live here and are NEVER committed (.gitignore).
TG_ARTIFACT_DIR=${HOME}/tmp/ds-test-guest
